  "notes": "West leads the ♠J against 6NT. West's spade lead is won by South. There are 10 top tricks (3 spades, 3 hearts, 3 diamonds, and the ♣A). North's diamond suit is the only possible source of 2 extra tricks.\n\nIf diamonds are 3-2, South can take all 13 tricks. If diamonds are 4-1, South can guarantee at least 12 tricks by finessing the ♦10 on the first round of the suit.\n\nThis safety play will not be good enough if West has all 5 diamonds. In this case, South must duck the first round of diamonds completely. When East shows out, the marked finesse against West's ♦J on the second round will ensure the contract.",
